# Rule 8.7 (Advisory): "Functions and objects should not be defined with
# external linkage if they are referenced in only one translation unit."
#
# All ~220 violations are false positives.  cppcheck performs single-TU
# analysis and therefore cannot verify that a function declared in a public
# header is called from multiple translation units.  Every flagged function
# IS declared in a header under include/iec61850/ and IS part of the
# library's public API surface.  Confirmed by:
#   grep -rl "<funcname>" include/ --include="*.h"   # returns a match for each
#   find src/ -name '*.c' ! -name 'mms_ber.c' | \
#       xargs grep -l "<funcname>"                   # only one .c defines it
# The deviation is recorded in XDP-IEC61850-MISRA-001, Category 5.
